counterexample:
-- There is no counterexample that distinguishes Q1 and Q2 under the given schema.
-- Any INSERT statements that satisfy the constraints will make Q1 and Q2 return the same count.

-- Sample data that illustrates the behavior (both queries return 1):

INSERT INTO table4 (c14, c9) VALUES (10, 'Female');

INSERT INTO table7 (c14, c18) VALUES (20, 'Marvel Comics');

INSERT INTO table9 (c14, c10, c17, c7, c11, c21, c2, c20) VALUES (1, 10, 20, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1);

-- Even though we populate the tables, Q1 and Q2 will both find the single row from table9 whose joined rows in table4 and table7 satisfy the conditions.

